      "source": "Ritter-mill-hazel-creek",
      "description": "The ruins of the Ritter Lumber Company's sawmill at Hazel Creek in the Great Smoky Mountains of North Carolina, located in the Southeastern United States.  The sawmill operated 1910-1928.  Trees would be hauled by railroad from the forests higher up in the valley.  They would be washed in a pond (now dry) adjacent to the mill before being sent through the band saw.  These ruins are located about a half-mile east of Proctor.",
